car fans rejoice as one of gaming's best  racing franchises is back with forza  horizon 5. the horizon series is known  for its more arcadey take on the forza  formula with gorgeous open worlds to  explore and a seemingly endless amount  to do 5 looks to be no different and is  the perfect time for new players to jump  in thanks to his day 1 availability on  xbox game pass here is everything to  know about forza horizon 5 and if you  enjoyed this video make sure to give us  a like and sub it really helps out  returning to develop is playground games  who yes are working on that new fable  but thankfully are large enough to  continue working on the horizon series  now horizon games are known for and  doing an amazing job of featuring  different parts of the world with each  title in three it was australia four was  the rainy countryside of great britain  and with five we're going to the lush  and varied mexico i say varied because  the game will feature 11 biomes  representing the different climates and  environments of the country we've got  canyon tropical coast rocky coast  jungle swamp sand desert living desert  volcano arid hills farmland and urban  that's a lot so much in fact that mexico  is the largest horizon map to date being  50 bigger than horizon 4. the team has  said they've taken great care to do  justice to the setting and stress that  they spent a lot of effort making sure  they don't play into any mexican  stereotypes this means working with a  mexican scriptwriter and a cultural  consultant creative director mike brown  said we want this to be a game that when  a mexican plays it they feel like it's  been made with care and love and i  really feel like we've taken this very  seriously to help mexico feel alive is  the return of seasons first introduced  in horizon 4. but this time things have  been anted up further with dynamic  weather weather is now local to a  specific region and you can see a storm  off in the distance and yes chase after  it if you wish i pray this eventually  leads to a twister themed dlc where i  get to live out the fantasy of being  bill paxton chasing after tornadoes  weather will be adapted based on both  the current season and the biome you are  in creating a much larger variety of  potential driving conditions but let's  talk about what you'll be doing in  mexico campaign mode returns this time  called horizon adventure your goal is to  get into the hall of fame which you do  by earning accolades there are a lot of  them with the idea being that you don't  have to earn all of them and instead can  focus on the types of challenges and  objectives you enjoyed the most as a  result horizon adventure is a lot less  rigid than previous horizon campaigns  there are 6 festivals in horizon 5 and  after the game's introduction you can  tackle them in any order you want this  is all part of the game's goal of giving  players more freedom as you explore the  map you'll naturally come across arcade  mini games the devs have compared these  to destiny's public events an arcade  event will spawn on the map you drive  over to it and will be grouped up with  other players online there are 12  different challenges and mini games they  are collaborative in nature such as  pinata pop where you work together to  destroy as many pinatas as you can or  bullseye where you need to jump off  ramps to hit the floating target the  horizon series has been pushing new  types of custom user created modes and  content over the years three introduced  blueprints and bucket list challenges  four added super seventh and five is  looking to take things even further with  event labs this is a new tool that lets  you create your own races and game mode  in many ways it looks to be forza's take  on halo's forge mode we've seen a small  sample of what event labs can do such as  this game mode where you have to run  into giant bowling pins but it won't be  until it's in the hands of the community  that its full potential will be revealed  the game's competitive multiplayer mode  previously called team adventure in  horizon 4 is now called horizon open the  change in name is to reflect the mode's  more accessible nature and removal of  skill based matchmaking don't worry that  doesn't mean there isn't any challenge  but playground games has expressed that  they just want the mode to be more fun  and casual for people to enjoy there  will be four playlists available in  horizon open open racing which offers a  variety of racing from street to cross  country open drifting for drift  challenges playground games for pvp  modes like flag rush and king of the  hill and finally returning in horizon  open is the eliminator forza's take on  battle royale the mode was added  post-release in horizon 4 and quickly  became the game's most played online  activity  horizon 5 has gotten an extra year of  development time compared to previous  entries and playground games has talked  about how this has allowed them to tweak  the driving to create a better  experience for example they've rebuilt  the way both suspension and brakes work  to feel more authentic and realistic  while realistic may sound like it's more  difficult in reality playground games  has said that this change has actually  made it more accessible and fun to drive  they've also talked about how they've  improved the experience when using a  racing wheel which should be great news  for all you die hards out there with  insane racing setups that i desperately  wish i had the space for and speaking of  die hards i know some of you love seeing  what real cars are available in these  games after all these are gorgeous cars  we can never have in real life but at  the very least we get to live that dream  in forza horizon 5's cover cars are the  mercedes amg 1 and the 2021 ford bronco  badlands other brand new cars to the  series include the 2020 toyota supra the  mark 1 ford escort the ford f-450 super  duty the porsche mccann rally raid and  the porsche taycan turbo s to name a few  on the customization end playground has  promised over 100 new rims 100 visual  upgrade parts thousands of performance  upgrades and the much requested ability  to paint your brake calipers there's  also the new audible upgrades which can  change the sounds of your car such as  the intake or exhaust character  customization is getting a much needed  boost you are still stuck with a  selection of preset faces but you can  now change your hair and hair color add  prosthetics pick your pronouns and voice  on top of having a greater pool of  clothing and accessories to work with  forza horizon 5 will be the first entry  on the new generation of consoles series  owners can expect a greater level of  detail in the environments and increase  draw distances thanks to the power of  the new systems ray tracing is supported  but only in forza vista the series mode  that lets you admire your cars up close  bit of a bummer but that doesn't mean  the game won't look gorgeous the rest of  the time the game features a new  volumetric lighting system and the  developers have talked about how they  have captured thousands of different  skybox photos at a whopping 12k  resolution so at the very least the  horizon  it's going to look pretty good series x  players can enjoy horizon 5 at 30 fps 4k  on quality mode and 60 fps 1080p on  performance mode meanwhile the series s  will run at 30 fps 1080p on quality mode  with a 60fps performance option  available as well the game will still be  available on xbox one systems as well as  pc we haven't seen how the game looks  and runs on xbox ones yet so maybe wait  and see before you try those versions  the great news is if you have xbox game  pass you've got the game available to  you on launch day november 9th but if  you are itching to play it four days  early you can upgrade to the premium  edition for 55 dollars might want to  start that download now though as it is  a whopping 102 gigabytes  yikes but if you don't have game pass or  want to wait and see how the game turns  out before spending all of those  gigabytes on the download make sure to  come back to gamespot for our full  review of forza horizon 5. thanks for  watching  you
 

